# Project: Life in Pixels — A Personal Life Journal and Daily Pixel Tracker

Act as a senior mobile application engineer, product designer, UX researcher, and design systems specialist.

Build a complete, production-quality mobile application called **Life in Pixels**.

The app transforms a person's life into a visual grid of days. Every day becomes a small, personalized pixel whose color is determined by the user's daily check-in. Each pixel can contain feelings, ratings, personal notes, memories, and optional photos.

Over time, the grid becomes a living visual record of the user's life: the good days, difficult days, ordinary days, meaningful moments, personal growth, and everything in between.

This is not merely a mood tracker, habit tracker, calendar, or notes application. Its defining experience is the connection between **daily reflection, meaningful personal records, and a beautiful long-term visualization of life**.

The app should feel intimate, thoughtful, calming, tactile, and worth returning to every day.

**Build a real, functional mobile application. Do not deliver only a landing page, static screens, or a Figma-like mockup.**

